 India, and, finally and unexpectedly, the inner peace and balance of love in Bali. Based on an inspiring true story, Eat Pray Love proves that there really is more than one way to let yourself go and see the world.","genres":["Drama","Comedy"]}],"info":[{"title":"Information","items":[{"title":"Studio","info":"Columbia Pictures, Eat Pray Love Productions, Inc.; Plan B Entertainment; Waveland Pictures Limited"},{"title":"Released","info":"2010"},{"title":"Run Time","info":"2 hr 23 min"},{"title":"Rated","info":"PG-13 for brief strong language, some sexual references and male rear nudity."},{"title":"Content Advisories","info":"Suggestive Dialogue, Language, Sexual Content"},{"title":"Region of Origin","info":"United States"},{"title":null,"info":"© 2010 Columbia Pictures Industries, Inc. All Rights Reserved."}]},{"title":"Languages","items":[{"title":"Original Audio","info":"English, English (United Kingdom), French, French (France), Italian"},{"title":"Audio","info":"English (AD, ⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC), French (France) (⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC), Italian (⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC), German (⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC), Japanese (⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC), Korean (AAC), Polish (⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC), Portuguese (Brazil) (⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC), Spanish (Latin America) (⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC), Spanish (Spain) (⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC)"},{"title":"Subtitles","info":"English (CC), Spanish (Latin America) "}]},{"title":"Accessibility","items":[{"title":"(cc)","info":"Closed captions (CC) refer to subtitles in the available language with the addition of relevant non-dialogue information."},{"title":"(ad)","info":"Audio descriptions (AD) refer to a narration track describing what is happening on screen, to provide context for those who are blind or have low vision."}]}]}